# Normalize line endings in the repository.
#
# Why: the working tree lives on a Windows drive and generated reports
# (data/analysis/**, data/validation/**) were written with CRLF. Because the
# index stored LF, every one of those files showed as modified even when the
# content was byte-identical, which left `git status` permanently dirty with
# ~1488 phantom changes and buried real work.
#
# `text=auto` normalizes to LF in the index; `eol=lf` checks LF back out.
# Git auto-detects binaries and leaves them alone, but the png rule is kept
# explicitly so image assets can never be mangled by content sniffing.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
